 | fields clients may set / never set | `validation.CLAIM_WRITABLE`, `validation.CLAIM_READ_ONLY` |
 | amount range, categories, roles | `validation.MAX_CLAIM_AMOUNT`, `CLAIM_CATEGORIES`, `EMPLOYEE_ROLES` |
 | actions shown on detail pages | `services.claim_actions` |
+| approval delegation (who stands in for whom, today) | `services.active_delegators` → `permissions.acts_as_manager_of` |
+
+### Approval delegation
+
+`delegations` (`delegator`, `delegate`, `starts_on`, `ends_on`) lets a manager hand their
+approval duties to another manager. A delegation is active on every date from `starts_on` to
+`ends_on` inclusive (the request's `X-Now` date). While active, the delegate can read, approve
+and reject the claims of the delegator's *direct reports*, exactly as the delegator can
+(`decided_by` = the delegate); the delegator keeps all rights. Rules:
+
+* only managers create delegations; `delegator` is the creator (sending it → 400); `delegate`
+  must be another existing employee with role `manager`; `ends_on` ≥ `starts_on` (else 400)
+* readable by delegator, delegate and finance; only the delegator can DELETE; PATCH → 403 for everyone
+* nobody approves or rejects their own claim, also not through a delegation (403)
+* delegations do not chain: rights come from the delegator's own direct reports only
+* an employee referenced by a delegation cannot be deleted (409), like one with claims or reports
 
